{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>An altar of earth.</b> Joined to the ground — that they not build it on pillars or on a pedestal. Another interpretation: he would fill the hollow of the bronze altar with earth at the time of their encamping (ibid.)." "<b>You shall make for Me.</b> That the beginning of its making be for My Name." "<b>And you shall sacrifice upon it.</b> Beside it, as in ״וְעָלָיו מַטֵּה מְנַשֶּׁה״ (Numbers 2). Or is it not rather literally upon it? Scripture states: ״הַבָּשָׂר וְהַדָּם עַל מִזְבַּח ה' אֱלֹהֶיךָ״ (Deuteronomy 12) — and slaughter is not on the top of the altar." "<b>Your burnt-offerings and your peace-offerings.</b> Which are from your flocks and your herd. (<b>Your flocks and your herd.</b> This explains ״אֶת עֹלֹתֶיךָ וְאֶת שְׁלָמֶיךָ״.)" "<b>In every place where I cause My Name to be mentioned.</b> Where I give you permission to mention My explicit Name — there <b>I will come to you and bless you</b> — I will rest My Presence upon you. From here you learn that permission was not given to mention the explicit Name except in a place where the Shechinah comes there, and that is the House of Election; there He gave permission to the priests to mention the explicit Name in the lifting of the hands to bless the people (Sotah 38)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:25.334727201Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}